n whips! But... Halberds? Man, that's such a cool and underrated weapon for video games! Ideal for pogos!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A Comicvania!</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comic art style blends into gameplay with a well integrated interface. The player is always in control in this comic book!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Our influences</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We got several influences from games we love, such as:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Half-Life 2 - Open storytelling, so the player is always playing!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Super Metroid - Great atmosphere in an interconnected world!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hollow Knight - Aerial combat through pogo-system!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Europa Universalis - Attention to detail when dealing with History!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comix Zone - A diegetic use of comic art style in order to bring a unique experience.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Commitment to historical fidelity</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Even though Plus Ultra: Legado is a fictional story with some supernatural events, we have made a strong research to accurately represent each civilization, character, and historical event. In fact, it has been translated into Nahuatl.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Colorfulness</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Most Metroidvanias are very dark. Which is great! But Plus Ultra: Legado wants to offer something different, something fresh.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Open storytelling</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Many sidescrolling video games force you to stop playing when a textbox appears. This is not the case of Plus Ultra: Legado. Move freely and even abandon story events if desired!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Find gold and buy upgrades</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are pieces of gold hidden all over this interconnected world. Traverse the land, explore each corner, and enhance your weapons.</p>","developers":["P\u00f3ntica